    tips: [
      { rule: ['Use I felt ... at first, but now I feel ... to describe a change in feelings. Use because to give a reason.', 'I felt ... at first, but now I feel ... で気持ちの変化を伝えられます。because で理由を加えましょう。'], examples: [['I felt nervous at first, but now I feel relaxed.', '最初は緊張しましたが、今は落ち着いています。'], ['I feel at home because I have good friends here.', 'ここには良い友達がいるので、居心地よく感じます。']] },
      { rule: ['Use I\'d like to + a verb for a future wish. Respond to a friend\'s plan and ask a follow-up question.', 'I\'d like to ＋ 動詞の原形で、これからしたいことを伝えられます。友達の予定にも反応し、関連する質問をしましょう。'], examples: [['I\'d like to take more photos with you.', 'また一緒に写真を撮りたいです。'], ['That sounds great. Where would you like to go?', 'いいですね。どこに行きたいですか。']] },
    ],
    apply: { situation: ['By the river, Claire asks Emma how she feels after the exhibition. Read their conversation.', '川のそばで、クレアが展示会を終えたエマの気持ちを尋ねます。二人の会話を読みましょう。'], roles: ['Claire', 'Emma'], dialogue: [['Claire', 'How do you feel after today, Emma?'], ['Emma', 'Happy. I was nervous at first, but everyone was so kind.'], ['Claire', 'What was your favorite moment?'], ['Emma', 'A visitor said my photos made her want to explore Kyoto.'], ['Claire', 'That is lovely. I\'m proud of all of us.'], ['Emma', 'Me too. Thank you for inviting me to be part of it.'], ['Claire', 'What would you like to do next?'], ['Emma', 'I\'d like to take more photos with Nao. How about you?'], ['Claire', 'I\'d like to organize another small event with everyone.'], ['Emma', 'I\'d love to help. Kyoto really feels like home now.']], questions: [['How did Emma feel at first?', 'Nervous.'], ['What was her favorite moment?', 'A visitor said the photos made her want to explore Kyoto.'], ['What would Emma like to do next?', 'Take more photos with Nao.']] },
    choose: [['I (felt / feel) nervous at first yesterday.', 'felt'], ['Now I (feel / felt) at home here.', 'feel'], ['I\'m proud (of / at) our work.', 'of'], ['Thank you for (helping / help) me.', 'helping'], ['I\'d like to (take / taking) more photos.', 'take'], ['I feel welcome (because / before) I have friends here.', 'because']],
    choices: [['A friend asks about your feelings. What do you say?', 'I felt nervous, but now I feel happy.', 'The counter is at three.', 'A'], ['A friend shares a future plan. How can you show interest?', 'No answer exists.', 'That sounds great. What would you like to do first?', 'B'], ['You want to thank a friend. What do you say?', 'Thank you for your support.', 'You should guess my feelings.', 'A'], ['You want to join a future project. What do you say?', 'Yesterday is a place.', 'I\'d love to help again.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma beside the river after the exhibition. Your tutor is Nao. You have time to talk about the event and what you would like to do next.', 'あなたは展示会の後、川のそばにいるエマ役です。講師はナオ役です。イベントやこれからしたいことを話す時間があります。'], task: ['Share one memorable moment and explain how your feelings changed. Thank Nao, ask about her experience, and agree on one thing you would like to do together next.', '心に残った出来事を一つ話し、気持ちがどう変わったか伝えましょう。ナオに感謝し、ナオの経験も尋ね、次に一緒にしたいことを一つ決めましょう。'], roles: ['Nao', 'Emma'], lines: ['Emma, I\'m glad we did the exhibition. What moment will you remember?', 'How did you feel before it opened? How do you feel now?', 'I loved hearing visitors talk about my ceramics. What would you like to ask me?', 'What would you like to do together next?', 'That sounds nice. When could we do it?'], evidence: 'Share an experience and feelings with a reason, thank the partner, ask a relevant question, and agree on a realistic future activity. Accept imagined experiences; do not demand emotional disclosure or a monologue.', useful: ['My favorite moment was ...', 'I felt ... at first, but now ...', 'Thank you for ...', 'How did you feel about ...?', 'I\'d like to ...', 'How about ...?'] },
